// Generated by examples/pom2k/generate_benchmarks.py. Do not edit; rerun the
// generator. Differential GPU (AMD, ROCm/HIP) test for ext_profv_: the pipeline
// output without the custom fusion pass (old), with it (new) and the native
// HIP reference (hip_ref.hip) run on identical inputs and are timed. Every
// array is compared between all three: old vs new bitwise, each against the
// HIP reference within a small tolerance (--rtol, --atol).
//
// --memory device (default): every array is a hipMalloc buffer. The inputs
// stay on the host and are copied in before every call, outside the timed
// region; the results are copied back for the comparison. This needs lowered
// code that never touches the arrays on the host, which run_diff_kernel.sh
// checks (lib/host_array_access.py) before running.
// --memory managed: hipMallocManaged arrays, for code that does touch them on
// the host. Without XNACK/HMM (e.g. ROCm on WSL) managed memory stays in host
// memory and the GPU reads it over PCIe, so its timings do not show GPU speed.
// The 1-element i32 selectors are managed in both modes: the lowered host code
// may read them to pick a branch.
